  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-07-26 from the merged FedID Digital Credentials draft: the static userAgentAllowsProtocol() method (unknown/disallowed protocol → false; ReferenceError only when an unguarded global DigitalCredential binding is absent), required request protocol members, readonly DigitalCredential.protocol, the DigitalCredentialProtocol union typedef, and its closed presentation and issuance enums. ChromeStatus “unspecified protocols” means arbitrary protocol identifiers outside the normative registry—not an omitted required member. Chrome 151 begins the flag-gated deprecation transition; removal is targeted for Chrome 160. The Chrome flag is #enable-experimental-web-platform-features; DigitalCredentialsProtocolFilter is the separate Finch/Blink runtime token. BCD availability (Chrome 141, Safari 26, Edge mirror, Firefox false) remains separate from that timeline. Substantive MDN check: API/DigitalCredential and userAgentAllowsProtocol_static both return 404 (Case B). Independent primary-source and browser review passed after correcting the protocol-filtering semantics, trial flag, typedef inventory, validation errors, and privacy constraints."
}
